# Trivy ignore list — each entry documents why the CVE is not actionable.
# Review quarterly; remove entries once upstream declares a patched range.

# CVE-2026-33671 — picomatch ReDoS (GHSA-qmt-xxm8-qqq4).
#
# The resolved version of picomatch in every node_modules/.../picomatch in
# the shipped image is 4.0.4 / 3.0.2 / 2.3.2 — all patched lines. Trivy's
# npm scanner, however, reads the SemVer range declarations in transitive
# packages' package.json (vitest, jest-util, jest-message-util all list
# "picomatch": "^4.0.3") and flags the lower bound of the range as the
# "installed version". This is a known Trivy behaviour — npm DB lookup by
# min-range-version.
#
# We keep the CVE ignored here rather than broadly disabling the library
# scanner; when vitest/jest bump their declared picomatch range to
# ^4.0.4 upstream, remove this entry.
CVE-2026-33671

# CVE-2026-102276, CVE-2026-102278 — brace-expansion DoS.
# CVE-2026-19534 — undici DoS via unrequested WebSocket.
#
# The same min-range-version behaviour described above, and the resolved
# versions in the shipped image are all patched. Trivy reports what the
# declarations say, not what npm installed:
#
#            Trivy "installed"   actually resolved   CVE fixed in
#   brace-expansion  5.0.9       5.0.12 and 1.1.21   5.0.10 / 1.1.19
#   undici           6.28.0      6.28.1, 7.29.1,     6.28.1 / 7.29.1
#                                8.10.2              / 8.10.2
#
# Verify with, rather than trusting this table:
#   python3 -c "import json;L=json.load(open('package-lock.json'));
#   print([(p,m['version']) for p,m in L['packages'].items()
#   if p.endswith(('node_modules/brace-expansion','node_modules/undici'))])"
#
# brace-expansion reached these versions in the same change that patched
# the npm-audit side of this batch (GHSA-6j4f-fj2g-mc7p and friends); the
# declaration lower bounds that Trivy reads live in transitive packages'
# package.json and cannot be moved from here. undici was already on a
# patched line and needed nothing.
#
# Remove each entry once the declaring packages raise their ranges.
CVE-2026-102276
CVE-2026-102278
CVE-2026-19534
